# Deepgram

- Master API key is server-only.
- Browser obtains a fresh short-lived temporary token from an authenticated endpoint immediately before every initial connection/reconnection and connects directly to Deepgram WebSocket. Use the 30s default TTL and consume immediately; never reuse a previous token for reconnect.
- The same server-side recording/transcription ConsentState gate applies before issuing either a Deepgram token or any fallback signed-upload capability. Revoked/invalid consent must deny both.
- Persist final transcript segments incrementally and idempotently.
- Implement reconnect states without duplicating text.
- Never send full audio/base64 through Next.js/Vercel.
- Batch fallback uploads directly to private Supabase Storage only after a server-issued upload grant; do not allow generic membership-only INSERT into the fallback-audio bucket. Backend receives object path/metadata only and transcribes by signed URL.
- Add retention/cleanup for fallback audio.
